# MeetingToText .dockerignore — repo-root context
#
# Build context is repo root (..) because both Dockerfiles use selective COPY
# (pyproject.toml + backend/, frontend/package.json + src/, etc.). This file
# is belt-and-braces to keep the context upload small — it does NOT break
# image builds because no Dockerfile depends on the excluded paths.
# Excluding data/models alone saves ~GBs; node_modules/dist saves 100s of MB.
.git/
.omo/
data/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
tests/
node_modules/
.pytest_cache/
**/__pycache__/
